    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so i am stuck on an iam policy issue. i have a lambda that needs to write logs to an s3 bucket but i keep getting access denied errors in the cloudwatch logs even though i think the policy is right. can you check this json for me?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\",\n        \"s3:GetBucketLocation\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your IAM policy only grants permission to AWS Lambda (the execution role), not to the CloudWatch Logs service profile itself. You need to attach this policy to the CloudWatch Logs role for your Lambda function, not just the Lambda execution role.\n\nYou should also verify that the S3 bucket policy explicitly grants `PutObject` permissions on the specific URI prefix you are attempting to write to, such as `arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/log_group/*`.\n\nFinally, check that the Lambda function's resource-based configuration identifies the correct log group name and that the log stream policy allows access at the stream level.",
